From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 16:35:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: qcom: add Surface Pro 11 platform support

Add the reviewed SP11 end state for touch and pen over HID-over-SPI and
QSPI, audio, volume keys, suspend mitigation, fan telemetry, and
platform profiles.

The SP11-specific touch/QSPI behavior was independently implemented from
public specifications, GPL-licensed Linux source, ACPI/device
information, hardware experiments, and WinDbg runtime observations on
the author's own licensed device. No Windows driver, firmware, trace,
captured descriptor fixture, decompilation output, or proprietary source
is included.

The private research history is intentionally not reproduced because it
contained unused descriptor-only diagnostic experiments. The preceding
eleven HID-over-SPI commits retain their original authorship, sign-offs,
copyright notices, and published specification reference.

Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
[omarchy: rebased onto 7.3. 7.3 already changes the Surface Pro 11 DMIC
rate (to 2400000), so the change to 3200000 is left out. The
spi-geni-qcom match table now carries .data, so the qcom,geni-qspi entry
points at geni_spi too and is_qspi is set after se.base. The
rx_dma_coherent unmap moved with the code into __spi_unmap_msg()]
